# Vintage ESPN App — what never goes in the repo.
#
# Two things here actually matter. The rest is housekeeping.
#
#  1. dynasty-data/ holds server.json, and server.json holds the access key
#     that is printed in your phone link. Anyone with it can read (and
#     generate on) your site while the app is running. Normally this folder
#     lives in AppData and is nowhere near the repo — but "portable mode"
#     (a portable.txt next to the .bat) deliberately puts it inside the app
#     folder, and that is how it would get committed by accident.
#
#  2. Dynasty archives are somebody's save history. Big, private, and
#     meaningless to anyone else.
#
# Your API key is NOT here because the app never writes it down: it is read
# from the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY environment variable at run time. Keep it that
# way — don't paste a key into a file in this folder.

# --- dependencies (npm install rebuilds these, and they are enormous)
node_modules/
package-lock.json.bak

# --- the data folder, wherever it ends up
dynasty-data/
portable.txt
**/server.json
*.incomplete-*
*.migrating

# --- a dynasty's own history
archive/
dynasty-*/
issues/
weeks/
prompts/y*/
state.json
.state/

# --- Codex trial reports (tools/codex-trial.mjs): full prompts and replies
codex-trial/

# --- run logs and rejected replies (diagnostics, often several MB)
*.log
_run-log.txt
_rejected-*.txt
team-images-usage.json

# --- local settings and editor noise
.env
.env.*
config.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- OS clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- build leftovers
*.zip
!branding-defaults/**/*.zip

# The photo library ships WITH the app, so it is deliberately NOT ignored.
# If the repo ever gets too heavy, uncomment the next line and hand the
# library out as a separate download instead.
# app/team-images-library/

# --- Madden port test material: copies of real saves and weeks shared for
# review (tools/share-week.ps1 adds review/ with -f when asked to)
fixtures/
review/

# --- the stadium ad library (app/ad-library): thumbs and catalog ship with the
# app; the full-size PNGs (156 MB) and the raw DDS export (1.4 GB) stay on the
# builder's PC. tools/ad-library-build.py rebuilds everything from raw/.
app/ad-library/png/
app/ad-library/raw/
